  <reason>Subject and account: The subject of this report is Zoya Akhtar, holder of account PK**ABPA****6053, opened on 17 July 2018. The customer's declared occupation is medical sales officer (salaried), with a declared income of PKR 220,000 per month.

Activity summary: During the period 2 March 2026 to 25 March 2026, the account recorded 11 credits totalling PKR 16,710,000 as well as 5 debits totalling PKR 15,352,000. The credits included 10 cash deposits totalling PKR 16,490,000, made over the counter at 3 branches (Clifton Branch, DHA Phase 6 Branch, Gulshan-e-Iqbal Branch). The activity was detected on 25 March 2026, when Tazama typology STR-PK-01 scored 320 against an alert threshold of 300.

Grounds for suspicion: 9 of 10 cash deposits (90%) were between PKR 1,600,000 and PKR 1,999,999, totalling PKR 16,004,000, just below the cash transaction reporting threshold of PKR 2,000,000. The cash was deposited across 3 branches (Clifton Branch, DHA Phase 6 Branch, Gulshan-e-Iqbal Branch) rather than at a single branch. The customer made more than one cash deposit on 1 day (20 March 2026). Credits in the activity window were 76.0 times the declared monthly income, against a declared income of PKR 220,000 per month. Taken together, these indicators are consistent with suspected structuring; the reporting entity has not established the underlying offence.

Flow of funds: Of the outgoing funds, PKR 15,352,000 was sent to Sheraz Traders (PK**SHER****1518, Synthetic Bank A) in 5 transactions. Funds did not remain in the account: debits equal to 92% of credits, with a median of 26.3 hours between the latest credit and each debit.

Other considerations: Screening of the subject returned no match on sanctions, PEP or adverse-media screening on 28 March 2026.

Action taken by the reporting entity: Action taken: a note by L2 analyst (28 March 2026): "Account placed under enhanced monitoring pending the reporting decision. No contact made with the customer about this review."</reason>
